		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: collision detection problem of collision shape controlled by haptic device]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=40242#p40242"><![CDATA[
A RigidBody will bounce off of a SoftBody, but the question is: what are you using to position the RigidBody onto the surface of the SoftBody?  If you're using a constraint to position it then of course: the constraint is stiff and will defeat any rebound effect from the SoftBody.<br><br>Perhaps you want to use a custom Action to push the RigidBody around so you can modulate how "hard" it tries to move?  I posted some example code for how to do this in <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?f=9&amp;t=11950" class="postlink">this thread</a>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11033">drleviathan</a> — Wed Dec 13, 2017 4:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
